    "final_answer": "## Task Completed Successfully\n\nI navigated to Apple's Repair page at **support.apple.com/repair** and found the following Apple Repair ways mentioned. I'll provide 2 of them as requested:\n\n### Two Apple Repair Ways:\n\n**1. Apple Retail Stores**\n- Apple retail stores offer Apple-certified repairs using genuine Apple parts. Repairs performed directly by Apple are covered by Apple's Limited Warranty and AppleCare plans.\n\n**2. Self Service Repair**\n- Self Service Repair is intended for individuals with the knowledge and experience to repair electronic devices. It provides access to genuine Apple parts, tools, and repair manuals to perform your own out-of-warranty repair.\n\n---\n\n**Additional repair ways also mentioned on the page (for reference):**\n- **Apple Authorized Service Providers** – A large network of certified providers offering Apple-certified repairs using genuine Apple parts.\n- **Independent, non-authorized repair providers** – Have access to genuine Apple parts and repair resources, but do not provide Apple-authorized repairs covered by Apple's Limited Warranty or AppleCare.\n\nSource: Apple Service and Repair page (https://support.apple.com/repair)",
